window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-989576428b6123b7"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"visualizations\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">可视化</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>可视化功能可以把问题、想法和信息转化为图表、地图、示意图、计算器、模拟演示和交互式说明，让你在 ChatGPT 对话中亲自探索。当调整输入内容或观察变量关系能让答案更容易理解、比较、练习或用于行动时，可以使用可视化。</p> <p>可视化功能目前正在逐步开放预览。是否可用可能取决于你的套餐、平台、账户和工作区设置。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>可视化预览正在逐步向 ChatGPT 桌面应用开放。当 <strong>Visualize（可视化）</strong>功能可用时，在输入框中键入 <code>@</code>，然后开始输入 <code>Visualize</code>，并在 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>下选择 <strong>Visualize</strong>。输入框会在你的请求前添加 <strong>Visualize</strong> 标签。</p> <p>如果没有看到 <strong>Visualize</strong>，请改用网页版 ChatGPT，或等预览功能开放到你的账户后再试。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在受支持的 Chat 或 ChatGPT Work 对话中，在输入框内键入 <code>@</code>，然后开始输入 <code>Visualize</code>，并在 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>下选择 <strong>Visualize</strong>。它的说明是 <strong>Create visualizations and interactive tools（创建可视化和交互式工具）</strong>。输入框会在你的请求前添加 <strong>Visualize</strong> 标签。</p> <p>你也可以输入 <code>@Visualize</code>，然后选择匹配的建议项。</p> <p><a id=\"check-availability\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">检查是否可用</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>使用界面</th> <th>当前可用情况</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>网页版 ChatGPT</td> <td>已向受支持账户的 Chat 和 ChatGPT Work 开放</td> </tr> <tr> <td>ChatGPT 桌面应用</td> <td>正在逐步开放预览</td> </tr> <tr> <td>ChatGPT 移动应用</td> <td>正在向符合条件的账户逐步开放；输入框控件可能因应用版本而异</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展</td> <td>不支持渲染可视化内容</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>如果你的账户已启用预览，可靠的判断标志是出现 <strong>Visualize</strong> 建议项。在逐步开放期间，即使套餐相同，不同账户、工作区和应用版本的可用情况也可能不同。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-when-a-visualization-helps\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">选择适合的可视化形式</h2> <p>当可视化能显著改善答案时，ChatGPT 可以自行选择合适的形式。如果你明确需要交互式结果，也可以添加 <code>@Visualize</code> 标签。</p> <p>请选择足以完成任务的最简单形式：</p> <ul> <li>要展示带标签的关系或流程，请使用示意图。</li> <li>要展示明确的数值数据和比较，请使用图表或曲线图。</li> <li>要展示地理信息，请使用地图。</li> <li>如果输入、时间、运动或空间关系需要变化，请使用交互式可视化。</li> <li>如果需要能够托管、可通过链接分享并保存数据的持久化应用，请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Site</a>。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"prompt-with-an-outcome-and-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">在请求中说明目标和控件</h2> <p>高质量的请求应说明目标、素材来源、要回答的问题，以及有用的交互方式。可以试试下面这个示例：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@Visualize how supply and demand determine a market price. Let me shift each curve, mark the equilibrium, and explain how price and quantity change.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：请用 @Visualize 展示供给和需求如何决定市场价格。让我移动供给曲线和需求曲线、标出均衡点，并解释价格和数量会如何变化。</p> </blockquote> <p>请告诉 ChatGPT 应使用哪些信息，例如对话中已有的内容、粘贴的数据、附件文件或可用的已连接来源。如果任务较复杂且可以选择推理设置，请选用更高的推理强度。</p> <p><a id=\"explore-interactive-examples\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">探索交互式示例</h2> <p>这些示例复现了 GPT-5.6 发布页面中的三个可视化。你可以操作控件，看看一个聚焦明确的提示词如何变成可交互的说明、实验室或教学工具。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：三个 ChatGPT 交互式可视化示例：带可调几何参数的万花尺图案（spirograph）、带可移动探针的波干涉实验，以及允许编辑文本并查看分词步骤的 tokenizer 说明工具。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"refine-and-continue\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">继续完善</h2> <p>在同一对话中继续说明你希望怎样修改。可以提出以下要求：</p> <ul> <li>添加或移除控件、筛选器、比较项或注释。</li> <li>修正源数据、单位、标签或假设。</li> <li>如果结果运行缓慢，可通过聚合、分箱或抽样简化处理。</li> <li>添加简短的文字摘要和数据表。</li> <li>让每个控件都能通过键盘操作，并显示清晰的焦点状态。</li> <li>除颜色外，也使用标签或图案区分内容，并移除循环播放的动画。</li> <li>如果需要托管并在之后重新查看，请将结果转换为 Site。</li> </ul> <p>后续请求可能会创建一个替代可视化，而不是直接修改原结果。在依赖新版本之前，请先检查它。</p> <p><a id=\"share-or-reuse-a-result\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">分享或重复使用结果</h2> <p><a id=\"add-a-visualization-to-a-page-in-space\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"space\">将可视化添加到 Space 页面</h3> <p>你也可以在 ChatGPT Space 页面中创建可视化。编辑页面时，输入 <code>/visualize</code> 和你的请求，然后选择匹配的菜单项。这样可以把交互式说明与笔记、研究资料或项目计划放在一起。示例请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d?anchor=add-interactive-visualizations\">在页面中添加交互式可视化</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"share-from-a-chat\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">从对话中分享</h3> <p>如果对话中提供了标准的 <strong>Share（分享）</strong>操作，就可以使用它。分享前请检查整段对话，包括源数据和更早的消息。可视化通常是 ChatGPT 创建时所用信息的一份快照，并非会与已连接来源保持同步的实时仪表板。</p> <p>生成结果中的下载控件和导出格式可能因结果而异。如果导出失败，可以要求 ChatGPT 用更简单的格式提供底层数据，或将可视化转为 Site。</p> <p><a id=\"improve-accessibility\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">改善无障碍体验</h2> <p>生成的可视化旨在使用语义清晰的控件、可见的焦点状态、易读的对比度并减少动态效果，但实际结果可能有所不同。分享前请检查可视化，并要求 ChatGPT 添加文字摘要和数据表、标明坐标轴和单位、避免只靠颜色传达信息，并确保控件可以通过键盘操作。</p> <p><a id=\"recover-from-a-failed-result\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">从失败结果中恢复</h2> <p>生成可视化可能需要一分钟或更久。如果结果为空白或没有显示，请等待回复完成，只重新加载一次对话，然后再试。如果仍然失败：</p> <ul> <li>要求生成更小或更简单的可视化。</li> <li>对数据进行聚合或分箱、减少抽样点，或降低大型数据集的精度。</li> <li>移除无法正常工作的生成控件或库。</li> <li>核实重要数值、地理边界和数据来源假设。</li> <li>改为请求图表、示意图、表格或 Site。</li> </ul> <p>处理数据时应遵循与你使用任何 ChatGPT 对话相同的判断标准。只有在组织政策允许的情况下才输入敏感信息，并在分享前检查完整对话。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">项目与对话</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1186da4cb8c2d6e2\">使用文件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">图像生成</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"visualizations\">Visualizations</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Visualizations turn questions, ideas, and information into charts, maps, diagrams, calculators, simulations, and interactive explanations you can explore in a ChatGPT chat. Use one when adjusting inputs or seeing a relationship would make an answer easier to understand, compare, practice, or act on.</p> <p>The Visualizations preview is rolling out. Availability can depend on your plan, platform, account, and workspace settings.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>The Visualizations preview is rolling out in the ChatGPT desktop app. When <strong>Visualize</strong> is available, type <code>@</code> in the composer, start entering <code>Visualize</code>, and select <strong>Visualize</strong> under <strong>Plugins</strong>. The composer adds a <strong>Visualize</strong> tag before your request.</p> <p>If <strong>Visualize</strong> doesn't appear, use ChatGPT on the web or try again after the preview reaches your account.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In a supported Chat or ChatGPT Work chat, type <code>@</code> in the composer, start entering <code>Visualize</code>, and select <strong>Visualize</strong> under <strong>Plugins</strong>. Its description is <strong>Create visualizations and interactive tools</strong>. The composer adds a <strong>Visualize</strong> tag before your request.</p> <p>You can also type <code>@Visualize</code> and select the matching suggestion.</p> <h2 id=\"check-availability\">Check availability</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Surface</th> <th>Current availability</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>ChatGPT on the web</td> <td>Available to supported accounts in Chat and ChatGPT Work</td> </tr> <tr> <td>ChatGPT desktop app</td> <td>Rolling out in preview</td> </tr> <tr> <td>ChatGPT mobile apps</td> <td>Rolling out to eligible accounts; composer controls can differ by app version</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex CLI and IDE extension</td> <td>Visualization rendering isn't supported</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>The <strong>Visualize</strong> suggestion is the reliable sign that the preview is enabled for your account. During the rollout, availability can differ across accounts, workspaces, and app versions, even on the same plan.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-when-a-visualization-helps\">Choose when a visualization helps</h2> <p>ChatGPT can choose a visual format when it materially improves the answer. You can also tag <code>@Visualize</code> when you specifically want an interactive result.</p> <p>Ask for the smallest format that fits the job:</p> <ul> <li>Use a diagram for labeled relationships or a process.</li> <li>Use a chart or plot for named numeric data and comparisons.</li> <li>Use a map for geographic information.</li> <li>Use an interactive visualization when inputs, time, motion, or spatial relationships should change.</li> <li>Use a <a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Site</a> when you need a durable hosted application with a shareable URL, permissions, or persistent data.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"prompt-with-an-outcome-and-controls\">Prompt with an outcome and controls</h2> <p>A strong request names the outcome, source material, question, and useful interactions. Try this example:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@Visualize how supply and demand determine a market price. Let me shift each curve, mark the equilibrium, and explain how price and quantity change.\n</code></pre> <p>Tell ChatGPT which information to use, such as content already in the chat, pasted data, an attached file, or an available connected source. For complex requests, choose a higher reasoning setting when one is available.</p> <h2 id=\"explore-interactive-examples\">Explore interactive examples</h2> <p>These examples reproduce three visualizations from the GPT-5.6 launch page. Use their controls to see how a focused prompt can become an interactive explanation, lab, or teaching tool.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Three interactive ChatGPT visualization examples: a spirograph with adjustable geometry, a wave interference lab with a movable probe, and a tokenizer explainer with editable text and tokenization steps.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"refine-and-continue\">Refine and continue</h2> <p>Continue in the same chat and describe the change you want. Useful follow-ups include:</p> <ul> <li>Add or remove a control, filter, comparison, or annotation.</li> <li>Correct the source data, units, labels, or assumptions.</li> <li>Simplify a slow result by aggregating, binning, or sampling the data.</li> <li>Add a concise text summary and a data table.</li> <li>Make every control keyboard accessible and add visible focus states.</li> <li>Use labels or patterns as well as color, and remove looping motion.</li> <li>Turn the result into a Site when it should be hosted and revisited.</li> </ul> <p>A follow-up can create a replacement visualization instead of editing the original result in place. Review the new version before relying on it.</p> <h2 id=\"share-or-reuse-a-result\">Share or reuse a result</h2> <h3 id=\"add-a-visualization-to-a-page-in-space\">Add a visualization to a page in Space</h3> <p>You can also create a visualization inside a page in ChatGPT Space. While editing the page, type <code>/visualize</code> followed by your request and choose the matching menu option. Use this to place an interactive explanation alongside your notes, research, or project plan. See <a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d?anchor=add-interactive-visualizations\">Add interactive visualizations to a page</a> for an example.</p> <h3 id=\"share-from-a-chat\">Share from a chat</h3> <p>Use the chat's standard <strong>Share</strong> action when it's available. Review the entire shared chat first, including its source data and earlier messages. A visualization is generally a snapshot of the information available when ChatGPT created it, not a live dashboard that stays synchronized with a connected source.</p> <p>Generated download controls and export formats can vary by result. If an export doesn't work, ask ChatGPT for the underlying data in a simpler format or ask it to turn the visualization into a Site.</p> <h2 id=\"improve-accessibility\">Improve accessibility</h2> <p>Generated visualizations aim to use semantic controls, visible focus, readable contrast, and reduced motion, but the result can vary. Check the visualization before sharing it. Ask ChatGPT to add a text summary and data table, label axes and units, avoid relying on color alone, and make controls work from a keyboard.</p> <h2 id=\"recover-from-a-failed-result\">Recover from a failed result</h2> <p>Visualizations can take a minute or longer to generate. If the result is blank or missing, wait for the response to finish, reload the chat once, and then retry. If it still fails:</p> <ul> <li>Ask for a smaller or simpler visualization.</li> <li>Aggregate or bin data, sample fewer points, or reduce precision in a large dataset.</li> <li>Remove a generated control or library that isn't working.</li> <li>Verify important values, geographic boundaries, and source assumptions.</li> <li>Ask for a chart, diagram, table, or Site instead.</li> </ul> <p>Use the same data-handling judgment you use for any ChatGPT chat. Only include sensitive information when your organization permits it, and review the full chat before you share it.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3c6726ad641677d6\">Sites</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">Projects and chats</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1186da4cb8c2d6e2\">Work with files</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">Image generation</a></li> </ul>"};
